  "info": {
    "sylid": 919,
    "subjectCode": "ENS211",
    "syllabusName": "SKILLFUL 2 - LISTENING & SPEAKING 1",
    "syllabusEnglish": null,
    "credits": "3",
    "degreeLevel": "Intermediate",
    "timeAllocation": "Hours Per Course: 30 sessions\n\n1 session = 90 minutes",
    "prerequisite": "Passed ENS111 and ENS121 (or equivalence)",
    "description": "Listening skill Upon completion of the course, students should be able to:\n\n- Predict with strategies - Listen for main ideas with language signals\n\n- Listen for examples /details - Listen for reasons/ time signals - Listen for comparisons / contrasts - Listen to summarize - Listen for vocabulary in context - Listen for opinions / cause and effect - Recognize oganizational phrases - Listen for problems and solutions - Listen for order of events/a process - Listen for details to add to a visual - Listen for pros and cons - Understand speaker's attitude - Listen to how an argument is supported Speaking skill Upon completion of the course, students should be able to: - Offer advice and suggestions - Encourage communiaction - Shift the topic - Ask for clarification - Agree and disagree - Explain something you don't know the word for - Manage questions - Be an effective public speaker - Use and refer to visual aids - Refute an argument Pronunciation skill Upon completion of the course, students should be able to: - Pronounce stress patterns, stress in compound nouns, sentence stress, emphatic stress and stress in words with suffixes - Fall or rise intonation in tag questions/conditional sentences - Link vowel sound and the same consonant sounds - Be aware of the schwa",
    "studentTasks": "- Attend more than 80% of contact hours in order to be accepted to the final examination\n\n- Actively participate in class activities\n\n- Fulfil tasks given by intructor after class\n\n- Use their own laptop in class only for learning purpose\n\n- Access the course website (http://cms.fpt.edu.vn) for up-to-date information and material of the course, for online supports from teachers and other students and for practice and assessment.",
    "tools": "Internet access",
